# Track 01 Execution Rules

## 1. Sequential Only — No Parallel Subagents

- Execute one phase at a time, in order (0 through 10).
- Never launch parallel Task/subagent workers for implementation.
- Waves 0–6 succeeded sequentially; Wave 7 does the same.
- Exception: readonly research (web search, doc fetch) may parallel.

## 2. Production-Grade — No Shortcuts

- Every file matches the staff-engineer bar of Waves 0–6.
- External calls: `withRetry`/`withTimeout`/`CircuitBreaker`/typed `AppError`.
- Money: integer paise, never float.
- Secrets: server-only, never client bundle, never git.
- UI: zinc+emerald, Geist, Phosphor, reduced-motion safe.
- Tools: Zod params, `runToolSafely`, fail-safe.
- Tests: CI-safe, deterministic.
- "It works" is not done. "Verified, tested, documented, pushed" is done.

## 3. Goal Awareness — Every Change Serves Track 01

- Before coding, re-read `.cursor/plans/track_01_upgrade_96eff3ff.plan.md`.
- Every change must serve: campaign orchestrator, conversational checkout, agent-readable catalog, upsell/cross-sell, audit trail, or graceful failure.
- Track 01 bar: every money action explainable, bounded, gated; audit trail; one failure handled.
- Do not build Track 02–04 or live ad-network integrations.

## 4. Use Skills Extensively

Read `.cursor/skills/README.md` at session start.

| Situation | Skill |
|-----------|-------|
| Any code change | self-review (silent, before presenting) |
| Any "done" claim | prove-it (gate output, not assertion) |
| New module / feature | grill first (resolve decisions) |
| Bug / failure | diagnose (reproduce → hypothesise → fix) |
| External API (Razorpay) | error-resilience (retry, circuit breaker) |
| Schema / migration | db-schema (queries-first, index every filter) |
| Git commit | git-workflow (atomic, conventional, push) |
| Performance | web-perf (measure first) |
| UI work | design-taste-frontend + ui-ux-pro-max |
| Agent tools | Follow defineTool + runToolSafely pattern from ADR 0004 |
| Long session (40+ calls) | session-guard (checkpoint, recite rules) |
| Before building | research-first-execution (check prior art) |

If a skill exists for the situation, READ its SKILL.md and FOLLOW it. Do not name-drop skills without invoking them.

## 5. Per-Phase Delivery Loop (12 Steps — Never Skip)

Every phase (0–10) runs this loop. No step is optional.

1. Implement the phase scope (complete, not a sketch)
2. Silent self-review (types, HMAC, RLS, no any, error paths, surrounding callers)
3. Write unit/integration tests for happy path AND edge cases
4. `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test`
5. If user-visible or public route: write/extend Playwright e2e; `npm run test:e2e`
6. Update Docs (module page + api.md + progress.md + learnings if gotcha)
7. `npm run build` (the real integration gate)
8. `git status` / `git diff` — confirm no secrets, one logical change
9. `git add`; conventional commit (`feat`/`fix`/`docs`/`test`/`refactor`/`chore`)
10. `git status` — clean
11. `git push origin HEAD`
12. Record evidence in `Docs/progress.md` (gate numbers, push)

If a gate fails: STOP, diagnose, fix, re-run full gate. Never push red.

## 6. Forbidden

- Do not launch subagents for implementation (readonly research only).
- Do not skip tests because "it's just a small change."
- Do not skip docs because "I'll do it later."
- Do not skip git push because "I'll batch commits."
- Do not use `any` as a type escape.
- Do not swallow errors silently.
- Do not put secrets in commits.
- Do not claim done without prove-it evidence.
- Do not modify frozen contracts (`errors.ts`, `resilience.ts`, `env.ts`, `agent/types.ts`, `research/standard-models.ts`) — extend via new files.
- Do not rewrite `0001_init.sql` or `0002_storage.sql`.
- Do not use float/number for money (integer paise only).
- Do not trust client-supplied amounts (server-priced SKUs).
